You are trading one soccer match in play. The market is the 1X2 result at the end of regulation time.
There are three contracts: home, draw and away. A contract pays $1 per share if its outcome is the result after 90 minutes plus stoppage time, otherwise $0. A level score is a draw. Extra time and penalty shootouts do not count.
Prices are dollars per share between 0 and 1 and are roughly the market's probability of each outcome. The three prices need not sum to exactly 1.
You hold either nothing or 1 share of one contract.
{% if config.fee_rate == 'market' %}
Costs: buying costs price + {{ config.half_spread|general }} + fee and selling returns price - {{ config.half_spread|general }} - fee. Fee per share = rate x price x (1 - price). Recorded market rates: {% for side, rate in config.market_fee_rates.items() %}{{ side }} {{ rate|general }}{{ ', ' if not loop.last else '.' }}{% endfor %}

A share held to the final whistle settles at $1 or $0 with no exit cost.
{% else %}
Costs: buying 1 share costs price + {{ config.half_spread|general }} + fee and selling returns price - {{ config.half_spread|general }} - fee, where fee = {{ config.fee_rate|general }} x price x (1 - price). At a price of 0.50 a buy costs {{ 0.5|buy(config)|compact }} and a sell returns {{ 0.5|sell(config)|compact }}, so buying and selling back loses {{ (0.5|buy(config) - 0.5|sell(config))|compact }}. A share held to the final whistle settles at $1 or $0 with no exit cost.
{% endif %}
